as a <strong>Python/Flask backend</strong>, you can't deploy the whole thing on Netlify.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Here are your options:</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Option 1 — Best for you: Render (free)</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Hosts Flask apps for free, easiest setup.</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to <a class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://render.com/">render.com</a></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Connect your GitHub repo</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Set build command: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">pip install -r requirements.txt</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Set start command: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">python app.py</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Done ✅</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Option 2 — Streamlit Cloud (if using Streamlit)</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">If your app uses Streamlit instead of Flask:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to <a class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://streamlit.io/cloud">streamlit.io/cloud</a></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Connect GitHub repo → deploy in 2 minutes</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Option 3 — Split deployment</h3>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Frontend</strong> (HTML/CSS/JS) → Netlify</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Backend</strong> (Flask/Python) → Render</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Frontend calls backend API</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Option 4 — Hugging Face Spaces (great for ML projects)</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Perfect for ML/AI projects, free, and looks great on resume:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to <a class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://huggingface.co/spaces">huggingface.co/spaces</a></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Supports Flask and Streamlit</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Very popular for ML portfolios</li>
</ul>
